    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The research plan clearly establishes a Hold stance, and the evidence supports this. AAPL is a high-quality, cash-generative franchise ($62.6B six-month operating cash flow) trading in a clear uptrend above all major moving averages, but it sits at a 60-day peak of $190.43 with decelerating momentum (negative MACD histogram for three days, RSI spiked 8 points in 8 days). The risk-reward of initiating fresh capital at this level is asymmetric to the downside, while the near-term AI catalysts cited by the bull are not verifiable from the supplied evidence block. This balances between a quality business and a stretched entry point, so I maintain existing positions without chasing at $190.43. I would set a protective stop below the 20 SMA at approximately $185.96, and reassess the thesis if the stock breaks below $185 toward the 50 SMA at $175.34.\n\n**Entry Price**: 187.0\n\n**Stop Loss**: 185.96\n\n**Position Sizing**: Moderate \u2014 keep new exposure limited; scale in gradually on pullbacks toward $186-$188, add more aggressively only on a retest of $175-$180 support.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
